WEBVTT

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.721
This is an impacted lower wisdom tooth.

00:00:03.971 --> 00:00:06.425
Its roots wrap around a nerve.

00:00:06.675 --> 00:00:11.453
Taking the tooth out can damage the nerve and make your lip and chin numb.

00:00:11.953 --> 00:00:14.193
The red part is the nerve.

00:00:14.443 --> 00:00:18.241
It gives feeling to the lower teeth, gums, lip and chin.

00:00:18.741 --> 00:00:22.602
As the tooth comes out, the nerve can be pressed or cut.

00:00:22.852 --> 00:00:26.948
The feeling often comes back, but sometimes it never does.

00:00:27.448 --> 00:00:32.205
Rates vary, but about 7 in 100 may get nerve damage.

00:00:32.455 --> 00:00:36.893
1 in 100 may have damage that does not go away.

00:00:37.393 --> 00:00:39.125
For a tooth like this,

00:00:39.125 --> 00:00:44.006
it is a good idea to see a specialist (an oral surgeon) first.
